#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# since: spec-v0.1
# features: [move, liveness, loop]
# doc: |
#   RV-F #14 (for-var MoveInLoop, REJECT direction). The `for`-element variable
#   `x` aliases persistent collection storage — it is NOT re-created each
#   iteration — so moving it out with `consume(!x)` would move OUT of the
#   collection: E_MoveInLoop. The oracle previously treated the for-element bind
#   as a body-local (loop-local) and wrongly ACCEPTED this; the fix keys on the
#   TYPED for-desugar view (`Source::BorrowView`), which is never loop-local.
#   stdout stays EXACTLY empty (the program never ran, which IS the verdict),
#   exit 1. This is the REJECT complement of loop_body_local_move_ok.gg (a genuine
#   body-local IS movable); flipping the expected `reject:` code must make every
#   lane MISMATCH (Core #6/#8). The 2-element iterable makes the re-move a genuine
#   multi-iteration reject, never a run-once loop.
# expect:
#   exit: 1
#   stdout: ""
#   reject: E_MoveInLoop
#!end

void consume(String !s):
    pass

void main():
    Vector[String] items = ["a", "b"]
    for x in items:
        consume(!x)
